# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOLD: do not enable this plugin yet.
#
# It is the first intake that carries text a stranger wrote into an
# agent that runs with your git credentials, can push, and has
# unrestricted network egress. That combination, an agent holding
# elevated credentials while reading untrusted input, is the 2026
# supply-chain pattern (Clinejection, RoguePilot): a payload in an issue
# title reaching a published package, hidden comments making an agent
# leak its token. Forge quotes the issue body and tells the model it is
# data, which is a mitigation, not a boundary.
#
# The boundary is item 1 of docs/GTM.md: each attempt in its own
# container, egress limited to what the task declares, credentials
# scoped to the task and expired when it ends. Enable this plugin after
# that lands, or only against a repository whose issues only you can
# open.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Copy this file to "config" next to plugin.toml (or into the installed
# copy under FORGE2_HOME/plugins/github-issues/) and fill it in. It is
# shell, sourced by github-issues.sh: KEY=value lines, one per line.

# owner/name of the GitHub repository to watch. Required.
GH_REPO=owner/name

# Only open issues carrying this label are filed as tasks.
LABEL=forge

# Added to the issue when its task lands. Unset (the default) skips
# labeling.
#DONE_LABEL=forge-done

# How often to check GH_REPO for new issues, in seconds. Never less than
# 30, regardless of what is set here.
POLL_SECONDS=120

# Local path to the git repository new tasks are queued against.
# Required.
TARGET_REPO=/path/to/repo

# The workflow new tasks run (see `forge workflows`).
WORKFLOW=direct
